# What masa.life serves. `wrangler.jsonc` points the asset upload at the whole
# checkout, so without this file every deploy published .git/, the tooling
# scripts and the config (found 2026-09-30: /.git/HEAD and /wrangler.jsonc both
# answered 200). This is an allowlist: ignore everything, then let the site
# back in. A new top-level page or directory has to be added here to ship
# (anything under assets/ already does); a new tooling file stays off the site
# without anyone remembering to exclude it. `node scripts/check-assets.mjs`
# checks the result against wrangler before a deploy.
# (_headers, _redirects and this file are handled by Workers and never served.)
*
!/index.html
!/accessibility.html
!/llms.txt
!/robots.txt
!/sitemap.xml
!/assets/
!/assets/**
